PicoShell Assignment
################
description: A tiny UNIX shell with job control.
################

Files:

Makefile	# Compiles the shell program and helper programs
README		# This file
psh.c		# The shell program

# Little C programs that are called by the trace files
myspin.c	# Takes argument <n> and spins for <n> seconds
mysplit.c	# Forks a child that spins for <n> seconds
mystop.c        # Spins for <n> seconds and sends SIGTSTP to itself
myint.c         # Spins for <n> seconds and sends SIGINT to itself
test.sh         # Smoke tests for the shell

Build:

    make

Run:

    ./psh

Run without prompt for tests:

    ./psh -p

Built-in commands:

    quit        Exit the shell
    jobs        List active jobs
    bg <job>    Resume a stopped job in the background
    fg <job>    Resume a stopped/background job in the foreground

Job IDs use the form %1, %2, etc. Process IDs may also be used for bg/fg.

Examples:

    psh> ./myspin 5 &
    [1] (12345) ./myspin 5 &
    psh> jobs
    [1] (12345) Running ./myspin 5 &
    psh> fg %1

Test:

    make test

